 "root_cause": "Public page, available, history and run_report bypassed the SkillService admission/task owner. They could query after stop_accepting, exceed the declared eight admissions/two slots, and disappear from service drain when callers were cancelled. Model history reused the unowned public method, so adding a public owner also requires an internal already-admitted path.",
 "changes": [
  "Own all four public metadata queries from admission through result delivery using the existing _execute mechanism",
  "Reject closed/full service before the first repository query, with skills_busy/503 and existing retryability",
  "Extract the unchanged history body into _history for already-admitted model reads, preventing nested admission and shutdown rejection of admitted work",
  "Preserve public signatures, repository arguments, cursor/platform/report payloads, original repository errors and model history text",
  "Keep existing task shield, slot/admission budgets, write guards, lifecycle coordinator, parser and database implementation unchanged"
 ],
